      "writtenOn": "2021-06-04T01:59:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We enlarge the CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to 14 based on below request.\nNormally these buffers are used for VPU, GPU 2D or DPU 2D which only acceptable physical continue memory.\nAnd these buffers will allocated from CMA first, but then CMA use up it will allocate memory from system through alloc_pages(Gfp, order) API. So we request to enlarge the default CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to 14.\n1080p RGBA layer need 8MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 12).\n4K YUV layer need 16MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 13).\n4K RGBA layer need 32MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 14).",
      "parentUuid": "cea5c567_11f372d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5853f06c9a4ac52277cc3cb2b9e53e121071155e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "517b973f_a2999547",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-07T20:01:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just noticed this reply and the bug mentioned in the description is not assigned to anyone, so it is very easy to miss.\nAllocating alloc_pages(Gfp, order) with order\u003d\u003d14 has a very high chance to fail. If CMA gets exhausted easily on your system have you tried to setup a larger CMA area using \"cma\u003d\" kernel command-line parameter?",
      "parentUuid": "35b82b9e_0a8421a1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5853f06c9a4ac52277cc3cb2b9e53e121071155e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80624d3d_cce59cf7",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165870
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-08T01:59:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As IP or function limits, some memory is reverved for other purpose (such as share with MCU)and cannot be accessed in linux. So the whole memory linux can access has some holes. It is splited into several memory partition and cannot be used as larger contigious memory. So the memory is enough but CMA size limited. We need to enlarge CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to avoid failure when GPU allocate memory.",
      "parentUuid": "517b973f_a2999547",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5853f06c9a4ac52277cc3cb2b9e53e121071155e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2eca9783_6799eedf",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-08T21:57:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if I understand your reply correctly, you can\u0027t increase your CMA area because there are holes in the entire address space created by reserved areas and CMA needs contiguous memory that does not have any holes in it. So the size of your CMA area is limited by the largest contiguous area between these holes.\nIn this case, how about defining several CMA areas in your device tree? This would allow you to increase CMA.\n\nAnother possible alternative would be to dynamically preallocate several 14-order pages for this special use, which is viable if you the number of such buffers in use at the same time is limited.\n\nEither way, I don\u0027t think increasing CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER would really help much because buddy allocator easily breaks larger page order blocks to satisfy smaller order allocations and in high memory pressure case it should exhaust its high-order pages much fasted than CMA.",
      "parentUuid": "80624d3d_cce59cf7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5853f06c9a4ac52277cc3cb2b9e53e121071155e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "124382e9_30319099",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1140781
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T04:30:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hello Suren,\n\nThanks for your feedback.\nWe enlarge the CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to 14 based on below request.\nNormally these buffers are used for VPU, GPU 2D or DPU 2D which only acceptable physical continue memory as VPU and DPU2D not MMU can\u0027t handle virtual memory.\nAnd these buffers will allocated from CMA first, but when CMA use up it will allocate memory from system through alloc_pages(Gfp, order) API, configure CMA to larger it may still has the risk of CMA use up for corner case, currently we set a suitable CMA size based on the total DDR memory size. So we request to enlarge the default CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to 14 (default 11 is too small, only support 4MB continue memory) which allow allocate large continue memory from system memory. Based on my test I also found configure CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER to 14 help memory fragmentation issue when keep monkey test several days (while true;do monkey --pct-syskeys 0 -v 100000;done)\n1080p RGBA buffer need 8MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 12).\n4K YUV buffer need 16MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 13).\n4K RGBA buffer need 32MB memory (request CONFIG_FORCE_MAX_ZONEORDER 14).",
      "parentUuid": "2eca9783_6799eedf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 52,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "5853f06c9a4ac52277cc3cb2b9e53e121071155e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18a9f04f_83c278e4",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1157738
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-09T16:46:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This solution can not be accepted in GKI because it will affect all other vendors and changing max zone order will have noticeable side-effects (CMA uses it and with more orders there will be increase in splits/merges in the buddy allocator).\nThat\u0027s why I\u0027m suggesting alternative solutions in my comments. Please review and consider them instead of reiterating your request.\nAlso, please follow up on the questions asked in the associated bug: https://b.corp.google.com/issues/193071440#comment5",
      "parentUuid": "124382e9_30319099",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
